# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
# No claim is used in more than one statement, so there are no claim lines.
# No premise joins two claims that use one word in two senses.
# P2 says "rational figure" where the usual formula says "rational nature". It is odd, but P2 is the only statement that uses the phrase, so no sense shifts through it.
# In C, "nature" means kind of being, as in "human nature". No other statement uses the word, so it is not a bridge.
